 been moving to the left  and this includes  social issues uh this includes  cultural elements as well so while the  economics are always  reflexively what we might go to um  social attitudes have changed as well i  mean look at something like approval of  black lives matter  in 2017 if you polled white college  graduates do you support black lives  matter  29 said yes i do that same poll  right now has 40 percent of white  college graduates supporting black lives  matter that's an  increase of almost 33 percent remember  not 30 it's 11 percentage points  but about almost a third about 30  percent  that it appears significantly overrides  oh  my the top tax bracket is three points  lower  under the republican plan and so  that to me seems like a major  factor in what we've seen from  college-educated white voters  moving more to the democratic party  the other thing also that may be going  on is that  as people simply become more politically  aware  they make more rational decisions about  where they say  they align before tr one of the things  that  trump did and we saw it in  absolute record turnout in 2020. trump  getting way more votes than he got in  2016.  biden getting way more votes than anyone  has gotten um  so one of the things that we saw trump  do  for better or worse is engage a lot of  new people  and there are likely lots of  college-educated white voters  who are recently out of college who were  in some nominal way kind of following  the politics of their parents maybe  maybe you maybe had some really you know  21 22 20 year old  uh in college or college graduates that  in 2015  were republicans in some nominal way but  maybe they didn't vote for example as  they became more politically aware i'm  not using the term woke but as they  became more engaged in politics  during the trump era and they more  understood oh wait a second yeah i don't  know what my parents saw in the  republican party but i don't see it with  trump i'm going to become a  democrat for example um i think that  that's a factor as well that sometimes  you just have people who more  as they get more involved they  understand that whatever they were  nominally identifying with originally  really wasn't for them and so that may  be something you see in the numbers  that may not not actually reflect a  shift it may simply reflect a change  from not paying attention to paying  attention  some things to think about let me know  your thoughts on this one
 

